'' linux-x86_64: cva_list is SysV's '__va_list_tag[1]', and fbc mangles a BYVAL one as C's
'' adjusted parameter type, 'P13__va_list_tag', and a byref or pointed-to one as the array,
'' 'A1_13__va_list_tag'. Neither is EVER written as S<n>_, yet EVERY occurrence is a
'' candidate -- the byval one as ONE candidate -- while a reference or pointer to the array
'' is an ordinary candidate (Q's and W's S1_, U's S3_). Every line below is fbc's own symbol,
'' measured with fbc-modern -target linux-x86_64 -gen gcc -r (2026-11-19). tiko wrote R as
'' ...A1_13__va_list_tagS0_. The same source pins linux-arm64 in cva-list-mangle-linux-arm64.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target linux-x86_64 --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/cva-list-mangle.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1N1PERA1_13__va_list_tag"(
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1N1QERA1_13__va_list_tagS1_"(
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1N1REP13__va_list_tagP13__va_list_tag"(
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1N1SEP13__va_list_tagRA1_13__va_list_tag"(
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1N1TERA1_13__va_list_tagP13__va_list_tag"(
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1N1UEP13__va_list_tagP13__va_list_tagRA1_13__va_list_tagS3_"(
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1N1VEPA1_13__va_list_tagP13__va_list_tag"(
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"_ZN1N1WEPA1_13__va_list_tagS1_"(
